<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> This matchup is heavily play/draw
    dependent. Your primary objective is protecting basic mana production
    to consistently satisfy land drops through continuous land destruction
    (<a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Stone Rain"
        >Stone Rain</a
    >, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Pillage"
        >Pillage</a
    >). Aggressively mulligan vulnerable two-land hands if they
    lack basic mana development or early logistical filtration
    to insulate against early disruption.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Transition out fragile early
    creature interaction like <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    > in favor of high-impact finishers (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    >). Deploying <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
    > is strictly essential to dismantle their reliance on <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Rishadan Port">Rishadan Port</a
    > and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Wasteland">Wasteland</a
    >—even in configurations running our own factories, Web's
    asymmetric taxing advantage far outweighs any internal
    synergy sacrifice.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Tactical Considerations:</strong> Preserve at least 2–3
    copies of <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >; completely cutting spot removal creates lethal
    vulnerability against rapidly scaling aggressive beaters
    like <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Terravore">Terravore</a
    > or <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Ravenous Baluchitherium"
        >Ravenous Baluchitherium</a
    >. Evaluate your speed mechanics carefully: while some
    competitive strategists retain <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Frantic Search">Frantic Search</a
    > to dig through opposing taxing spheres, trimming high-cost filtration
    often stabilizes operational curve reliability.<br />
    <em>Advanced Tech Applications:</em>
    <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Divert"
        >Divert</a
    > serves as an exceptional pseudo-counterspell against targeted
    land destruction, while <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Sacred Ground">Sacred Ground</a
    > completely invalidates their destruction suite entirely.
</p>
